From 86785d400506bec885f73bcab18918c85f38693e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: devbotbo <7118.eth@proton.me>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 20:00:22 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Minimize GET /result/:id, gate plaintext behind RESULT_TOKEN,
 cap and expire bridge sessions

The result endpoint now serves a ResultSummary by default: vct, holder and
nonce binding, the age_equal_or_over predicate, the credential exp and the
disclosed claim paths. No disclosed string value and no presentation string
is kept after verification unless the operator turns on a flag.

RESULT_INCLUDES_PRESENTATION now defaults to false and serves the raw
presentation (the SP1 route's plaintext boundary). RESULT_INCLUDES_NAMES
(new, default false) serves the parsed view with its values. Either flag
requires RESULT_TOKEN: reads must carry a matching X-Result-Token header
(401 otherwise); with a flag on and no token configured the endpoint
answers 503 instead of serving plaintext. The wallet-facing and relay
endpoints stay unauthenticated.

POST /request sessions are capped (BRIDGE_MAX_PENDING, default 1000, 429
beyond) and dropped with their outcome after BRIDGE_SESSION_TTL_SECS
(default 900), pruned on the next POST /request.

Regression tests with synthetic data: no response carries the fixture's
given_name or family_name unless the flag is on and the token is presented;
missing or wrong token is 401, flag without token is 503; a relay session
never exposes plaintext; cap and TTL behave.
